*
* START-HISTORY:
* 25 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux 04f1eaa - the screen library as of S.75 TK-0.13 (containers and viewports, slider, selector, colour, accelerators, table styles)
* 12 Oct 26 dm  New.
* 18 Oct 26 dm  Containers and viewports ($sl_viewport): a widget may have a parent (w{'parent'} an id, w{'pn'} its
*               number), laid out from it, clipped to it, hidden / disabled / deleted with it; the ops scroll and delete;
*               the wheel, a drag on a bar's thumb, a child taking the focus scrolling into view, the hardware cursor
*               hidden while the focused widget is not wholly in view.  A form with no parents is drawn as before.
* 18 Oct 26 dm  Terminal 140 by 42, phase 3: the cursor is hidden and shown through $sl_curat, which also tells the cursor lock;
*               the key guardquit is not a widget's, and a modal form reads it as Esc.
* 18 Oct 26 dm  The op drawwidget: one widget drawn again, not the whole form (the IDE changing record rewrote the whole screen, which showed as a flash).
* 19 Oct 26 dm  wait.event: a null key is a timeout only when STATUS() is ER$TIMEOUT; an input that has ended is end, with or without a timeout
*               (the IDE's timeout 1 turned the end into timeouts for ever, at full CPU; sandbox-eofkeys.py).
* 19 Oct 26 dm  f{'bgclick'} = 1: a press of the left button on no widget comes back as the key mouse (SCREEN MOUSE says where) instead of
*               being ignored, so that the IDE can open its menu from a click on the bar.
* 22 Oct 26 dm  selector (S.75, TK-0.10): dispatched like the slider, and a change of its value is a change event.
* 22 Oct 26 dm  Accelerators (S.75, TK-0.12): find.accel and run.accel at the top of route.key; f{'achg'} makes the change event.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_form(op, f, scr, key, ret)      the widget contract (screenlib-design.md)
*
*   f is a data collection.  The elements of a form:
*
*     type     form                          title   shown in the top border
*     x y      its top left cell on the screen (null: centred)      w h   its size (null: the widgets' extent plus a margin)
*     widgets  an array of widget collections ($sl_label describes the ones every widget has)
*     focus    the number of the widget that has the focus (0 none)
*     shown    1 while the form is on the screen
*     curparent  the id SCREEN IN named: the widgets added now are inside that container (null: none)
*     drag     the number of the viewport whose scroll bar thumb the mouse is dragging (0 none)
*     scrolled the id of the viewport that was scrolled, then its sx, sy: WAIT turns it into a change event
*     curhid   1 while the form has hidden the cursor because the focused widget is not wholly in view
*
*   A widget is any of: label frame entry check slider selector radio list combo button progress tabs memo table tree scroll
*   container viewport.  It has x y,
*   its place from the top left corner of the form (0,0 is the corner of the border), and w h, its size, once its
*   own init has run.  disabled (1) takes it out of the focus ring.  page (a number, set by SCREEN PAGE through
*   $sl_wadd) puts it on one page of the form's tab strip: it is drawn, can have the focus and gets keys only while
*   the strip's chosen tab is that number (f{'page'}, which the form takes from the strip); a widget with no page is
*   on every page, and a form with no strip shows every widget.
*
*     init    fills in the form's own elements (and the size and place, if left out)
*     find    key is a widget id; ret is its number, 0 if there is none
*     draw    the frame, then every widget, the focused one last (it leaves the cursor in itself)
*     drawwidget  key is a widget id: that one widget is drawn again, and the cursor goes back to the focused widget (no frame,
*             no other widget; nothing if the form is not shown)
*     focus   key is a widget id (or number); the focus goes there, both widgets redrawn
*     key     one key goes to the widget that has the focus.  ret<1> is 'handled', 'done' or 'cancel'
*             (ret<2> the id of the button that ended the form; for Esc, that of the form's cancel
*             button or null), or 'unhandled' with ret<2> the key.
*     run     modal: saves what is under the form, draws it, reads keys until done or cancel, puts the
*             screen back.  ret as for key.
*     close   puts the screen back if the form is shown (run does this itself)
*     scroll  key is a viewport's id: its sx, sy (set by the caller) are brought into range and, if the form is shown,
*             the viewport and what is in it drawn again.  ret is sx, a value mark, sy; null if there is no such viewport
*     delete  key is a widget id: the widget and, if it is a container, everything inside it are taken out of the form
*             (drawn again if shown).  ret is how many were taken out
*     layout  the widgets' places on the screen worked out again (a widget's ax, ay and, for the ones that have a
*             container, the clip they are drawn and hit in)
*
*   A container's children are laid out from it: a child's place is the container's inner origin (the first cell inside
*   its border, less the viewport's scroll) plus the child's x, y.  They come after it in the array, so the container is
*   drawn first.  Whatever a child does is cut to the visible part of its container and of the containers outside that.
*
*   Keys the form acts on itself when the widget does not use them: Tab and Down go to the next widget
*   that can have the focus, Shift-Tab and Up to the one before (round the ring); Return presses the
*   form's default button wherever the focus is (it presses a button that has the focus whether or not it
*   is the default), and without a default button goes to the next widget; Esc is cancel; a letter is the
*   mnemonic of a button, which is pressed.
*
*   Accelerators (S.75 TK-0.12): a control given ACCEL 'alt-s' (or f1 to f12, ctrl-a to ctrl-z, alt-a to alt-z, alt-0 to alt-9) gets that key wherever the
*   focus is, even in a text field, before the focused control sees it.  An Alt-letter is also the letter marked with & in the text of a button, check
*   box, slider, selector or label.  The first such control in the order they were added, on the page and not disabled, takes the key: a button is pressed,
*   a check box, slider or selector is turned over (a selector goes to its next word; a change event is made), a label moves the focus to the next control
*   that can have it, and any other control just takes the focus.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_form(op, f, scr, key, ret)
$catalog $sl_form

$include sl.h
$include err.h

   ret = ''
   wkey = ''                                 ;* the key handed to a widget: none for init, draw ...
   scr<SL.S.DIFF> = scr<SL.S.SYNC> + 0       ;* 19 Oct 26: on a screen the terminal of which is known to match its shadow, $sl_put leaves out what is shown already

   begin case
      case op = 'init'
         gosub init.form

      case op = 'find'
         id = key
         gosub find.widget
         ret = fw

      case op = 'draw'
         gosub init.form
         gosub layout
         gosub draw.all

      case op = 'focus'
         id = key
         gosub find.widget
         if fw = 0 and num(key) then fw = key + 0
         nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
         if fw >= 1 and fw <= nw then
            ni = fw
            gosub set.focus
         end

      case op = 'key'
         gosub route.key

      case op = 'run'
         gosub run.modal

      case op = 'wait'
         tmo = key
         gosub wait.event

      case op = 'hide' or op = 'close'
         gosub hide.form

      case op = 'redraw'
         if f{'shown'} then
            gosub init.page
            gosub layout
            gosub draw.all
         end

      case op = 'drawwidget'
         * 18 Oct 26: key is a widget id: that widget alone is drawn again (where it is, as the last layout left it), and the cursor
         * goes back to the focused widget.  A program that changed one widget need not repaint the whole form (every cell of the
         * screen written again is seen as a flash).  Nothing if the form is not shown or there is no such widget.
         if f{'shown'} then
            id = key
            gosub find.widget
            if fw > 0 then
               di = fw
               gosub draw.one
               gosub park.cursor
            end
         end

      case op = 'layout'
         gosub init.page
         gosub layout

      case op = 'scroll'
         id = key
         gosub find.widget
         if fw > 0 then
            w = f{'widgets', fw}
            if w{'type'} = 'viewport' then
               call $sl_viewport('geom', w, scr, '', r)
               ret = w{'sx'} : @vm : w{'sy'}
               if f{'shown'} then
                  vi = fw
                  gosub redraw.vp
               end
            end
         end

      case op = 'delete'
         id = key
         gosub find.widget
         if fw > 0 then gosub delete.widget
   end case

   scr<SL.S.DIFF> = 0

   return

* Put the screen back if the form is shown
hide.form:
   if f{'shown'} then
      under = f{'under'}
      call $sl_region('restore', scr, f{'x'} + 0, f{'y'} + 0, f{'w'} + 0, f{'h'} + 0, under)
      f{'shown'} = 0
      gosub show.cursor
   end
   return

* The cursor the form hid (park.cursor) is shown again, if the screen's own state says it is on
show.cursor:
   if f{'curhid'} + 0 then
      f{'curhid'} = 0
      if scr<SL.S.CURON> then
         display @(-31) :
         call $sl_curat('on', '')
      end
   end
   return

* The form's own elements, and a size and a place if there are none
init.form:
   f{'type'} = 'form'
   if jtype(f{'widgets'}) # 'array' then f{'widgets'} = mat()
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   if f{'w'} = '' or f{'h'} = '' then
      maxr = len(f{'title'}) + 6
      maxb = 3
      for i = 1 to nw
         w = f{'widgets', i}
         if w{'pn'} + 0 = 0 then                 ;* a widget inside a container is placed in the container, not in the form
            if w{'x'} + w{'w'} + 2 > maxr then maxr = w{'x'} + w{'w'} + 2
            if w{'y'} + w{'h'} + 2 > maxb then maxb = w{'y'} + w{'h'} + 2
         end
      next i
      if f{'w'} = '' then f{'w'} = maxr
      if f{'h'} = '' then f{'h'} = maxb
   end
   if f{'x'} = '' then f{'x'} = int((scr<SL.S.W> - f{'w'}) / 2)
   if f{'y'} = '' then f{'y'} = int((scr<SL.S.H> - f{'h'}) / 2)
   gosub init.page
   return

* The page the form shows is the chosen tab of its tab strip; with no strip every widget shows
init.page:
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      if w{'type'} = 'tabs' then f{'page'} = w{'value'} ; exit
   next i
   return

* vis = 1 if widget w is on the page the form shows (a widget that has no page is on every page) and is not hidden;
* ancdis = 1 if a container above it is disabled.  A container's page, hiding and disabling hold for what is in it.
on.page:
   pg = w{'page'} + 0
   vis = (pg = 0 or f{'page'} = '' or pg = f{'page'} + 0)
   if w{'hidden'} + 0 then vis = 0            ;* SCREEN SET ... VISIBLE 0
   ancdis = 0
   pq = w{'pn'} + 0
   for pk = 1 to 32
      if pq = 0 then exit
      pw = f{'widgets', pq}
      pg = pw{'page'} + 0
      if not(pg = 0 or f{'page'} = '' or pg = f{'page'} + 0) then vis = 0
      if pw{'hidden'} + 0 then vis = 0
      if pw{'disabled'} + 0 then ancdis = 1
      pq = pw{'pn'} + 0
   next pk
   return

* Every widget's place on the screen.  A widget in a container is placed from the container's inner origin (ox, oy: the
* first cell inside its border, less a viewport's scroll) and cut to its visible part (clip: x0 y0 x1 y1 as values); a
* container is laid out before what is in it because it comes first in the array.
layout:
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   for li = 1 to nw
      lw = f{'widgets', li}
      lq = lw{'pn'} + 0
      if lq > 0 then
         lp = f{'widgets', lq}
         lw{'ax'} = lp{'ox'} + lw{'x'}
         lw{'ay'} = lp{'oy'} + lw{'y'}
         lw{'clip'} = lp{'cl'}
      end else
         lw{'ax'} = f{'x'} + lw{'x'}
         lw{'ay'} = f{'y'} + lw{'y'}
         lw{'clip'} = ''
      end
      ltyp = lw{'type'}
      if ltyp = 'container' or ltyp = 'viewport' then gosub layout.container
   next li
   return

* The container lw (placed, with its own clip): the origin of what is in it, and the part of the inside that shows
layout.container:
   call $sl_viewport('geom', lw, scr, '', lr)
   cb = lw{'bw'} + 0
   cx0 = lw{'ax'} + cb
   cy0 = lw{'ay'} + cb
   lw{'ox'} = cx0 - lw{'sx'}
   lw{'oy'} = cy0 - lw{'sy'}
   cx1 = cx0 + lw{'visw'} - 1
   cy1 = cy0 + lw{'vish'} - 1
   lc = lw{'clip'}
   if lc # '' then
      if lc<1, 1> > cx0 then cx0 = lc<1, 1>
      if lc<1, 2> > cy0 then cy0 = lc<1, 2>
      if lc<1, 3> < cx1 then cx1 = lc<1, 3>
      if lc<1, 4> < cy1 then cy1 = lc<1, 4>
   end
   lw{'cl'} = cx0 : @vm : cy0 : @vm : cx1 : @vm : cy1
   return

* outside = 1 if no cell of widget w is inside the clip it has from its containers
clipped.out:
   outside = 0
   cc = w{'clip'}
   if cc # '' then
      if w{'ax'} > cc<1, 3> or w{'ax'} + w{'w'} - 1 < cc<1, 1> or w{'ay'} > cc<1, 4> or w{'ay'} + w{'h'} - 1 < cc<1, 2> then outside = 1
   end
   return

* The inside of the container w is blanked in the form's style, within the part of it that shows
blank.inside:
   cc = w{'cl'}
   if cc<1, 3> >= cc<1, 1> and cc<1, 4> >= cc<1, 2> then
      call $sl_attr('window', bc)
      for br = cc<1, 2> to cc<1, 4>
         call $sl_put(scr, cc<1, 1> + 0, br, space(cc<1, 3> - cc<1, 1> + 1), bc)
      next br
   end
   return

draw.all:
   call $sl_attr('window', nc)
   call $sl_frame(scr, f{'x'} + 0, f{'y'} + 0, f{'w'} + 0, f{'h'} + 0, f{'title'}, nc, 1)
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   fi = f{'focus'} + 0
   for i = 1 to nw
      if i # fi then
         di = i
         gosub draw.one
      end
   next i
   if fi >= 1 and fi <= nw then
      di = fi
      gosub draw.one
   end
   gosub park.cursor
   return

* Draw widget number di, if it is on the page and any of it is where it can be seen.  A container is blanked inside first
* unless it has the focus (it is drawn last then, over what is in it).
draw.one:
   w = f{'widgets', di}
   gosub on.page
   if vis then
      gosub clipped.out
      if outside = 0 then
         wt = w{'type'}
         if (wt = 'container' or wt = 'viewport') and di # f{'focus'} + 0 then gosub blank.inside
         wop = 'draw'
         gosub call.widget
      end
   end
   return

* The hardware cursor belongs to the focused widget, which puts it where its text is.  If the widget is a container
* (it takes no text), or is not wholly where it can be seen (a viewport has scrolled it away, or it is hidden), the
* cursor would sit on something else: it is hidden, and shown again when the widget is back in view.
park.cursor:
   pfi = f{'focus'} + 0
   phide = 0
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   if pfi >= 1 and pfi <= nw then
      if unassigned(w) then pw0 = '' else pw0 = w
      w = f{'widgets', pfi}
      pt = w{'type'}
      pc = w{'clip'}
      if pt = 'container' or pt = 'viewport' then
         phide = 1
      end else
         if pc # '' then
            gosub on.page
            if vis = 0 then phide = 1
            if w{'ax'} < pc<1, 1> or w{'ax'} + w{'w'} - 1 > pc<1, 3> or w{'ay'} < pc<1, 2> or w{'ay'} + w{'h'} - 1 > pc<1, 4> then phide = 1
         end
      end
      w = pw0
   end
   if phide then
      display @(-32) :
      call $sl_curat('off', '')
      f{'curhid'} = 1
   end else
      gosub show.cursor
   end
   return

* id = a widget id; fw = its number, 0 if there is none
find.widget:
   fw = 0
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      if w{'id'} = id then fw = i ; exit
   next i
   return

* Run one operation of one widget: wop, w (a widget collection), wt (its type), wkey.  wr is the answer.
* A widget in a container is run with the clip narrowed to the part of the container that shows (the program's own clip
* kept in SL.S.BCLIP, for the pop-ups a widget opens); vmoved is 1 afterwards if the widget was a viewport that scrolled.
call.widget:
   wr = ''
   vmoved = 0
   wcl = w{'clip'}
   nrw = (wcl # '')
   if nrw then
      sclip = scr<SL.S.CLIP>
      nx0 = wcl<1, 1> ; ny0 = wcl<1, 2> ; nx1 = wcl<1, 3> ; ny1 = wcl<1, 4>
      if sclip # '' then
         if sclip<1, 1> > nx0 then nx0 = sclip<1, 1>
         if sclip<1, 2> > ny0 then ny0 = sclip<1, 2>
         if sclip<1, 3> < nx1 then nx1 = sclip<1, 3>
         if sclip<1, 4> < ny1 then ny1 = sclip<1, 4>
      end
      scr<SL.S.BCLIP> = sclip
      scr<SL.S.NARROW> = 1
      scr<SL.S.CLIP> = nx0 : @vm : ny0 : @vm : nx1 : @vm : ny1
   end
   if wt = 'viewport' then
      vsx0 = w{'sx'} + 0
      vsy0 = w{'sy'} + 0
   end
   begin case
      case wt = 'entry' ; call $sl_entry(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'list' ; call $sl_list(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'check' ; call $sl_check(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'slider' ; call $sl_slider(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'selector' ; call $sl_selector(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'radio' ; call $sl_radio(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'button' ; call $sl_button(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'label' ; call $sl_label(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'combo' ; call $sl_combo(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'progress' ; call $sl_progress(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'tabs' ; call $sl_tabs(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'memo' ; call $sl_memo(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'table' ; call $sl_table(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'tree' ; call $sl_tree(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'scroll' ; call $sl_scroll(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'container' or wt = 'viewport' ; call $sl_viewport(wop, w, scr, wkey, wr)
      case wt = 'frame'
         if wop = 'draw' then
            call $sl_attr('window', wc)
            call $sl_frame(scr, w{'ax'} + 0, w{'ay'} + 0, w{'w'} + 0, w{'h'} + 0, w{'title'}, wc, 0)
         end
      case 1
         wr = 'unhandled' : @fm : wkey
   end case
   if nrw then
      scr<SL.S.CLIP> = sclip
      scr<SL.S.BCLIP> = ''
      scr<SL.S.NARROW> = 0
   end
   if wt = 'viewport' then
      if w{'sx'} + 0 # vsx0 or w{'sy'} + 0 # vsy0 then vmoved = 1
   end
   return

* A widget can have the focus if it takes keys at all and is not disabled (nor is a container it is in), and is on the page
can.focus:
   w = f{'widgets', i}
   gosub on.page
   cf = (w{'focusable'} + 0 = 1 and w{'disabled'} + 0 = 0 and ancdis = 0 and vis)
   return

* The focus goes to widget number ni; the one that had it is redrawn without
set.focus:
   old = f{'focus'} + 0
   if old >= 1 and old <= nw and old # ni then
      w = f{'widgets', old}
      wt = w{'type'}
      wop = 'focus' ; wkey = 0
      gosub call.widget
   end
   f{'focus'} = ni
   w = f{'widgets', ni}
   if w{'pn'} + 0 > 0 and f{'shown'} then
      * a widget in a viewport comes into view; the viewports that moved are drawn again before the widget is
      gosub reveal
      if rvi > 0 then
         vi = rvi
         gosub redraw.vp
         w = f{'widgets', ni}
      end
   end
   wt = w{'type'}
   wop = 'focus' ; wkey = 1
   gosub call.widget
   gosub park.cursor
   return

* The widget w (number ni) is to be seen: every viewport it is in is scrolled just far enough that the widget is inside what
* shows (a widget too big for the window has its top left corner shown).  rvi = the outermost viewport that moved, 0 if none.
reveal:
   rvi = 0
   rvw = w
   rpi = w{'pn'} + 0
   for rk = 1 to 32
      if rpi = 0 then exit
      rvp = f{'widgets', rpi}
      if rvp{'type'} = 'viewport' then
         call $sl_viewport('geom', rvp, scr, '', rr)
         tx = rvw{'ax'} - rvp{'ox'}
         ty = rvw{'ay'} - rvp{'oy'}
         tw = rvw{'w'} + 0
         th = rvw{'h'} + 0
         rsx = rvp{'sx'} + 0
         rsy = rvp{'sy'} + 0
         begin case
            case tx < rsx
               rsx = tx
            case tx + tw > rsx + rvp{'visw'}
               rsx = tx + tw - rvp{'visw'}
               if rsx > tx then rsx = tx
         end case
         begin case
            case ty < rsy
               rsy = ty
            case ty + th > rsy + rvp{'vish'}
               rsy = ty + th - rvp{'vish'}
               if rsy > ty then rsy = ty
         end case
         if rsx # rvp{'sx'} + 0 or rsy # rvp{'sy'} + 0 then
            rvp{'sx'} = rsx
            rvp{'sy'} = rsy
            call $sl_viewport('geom', rvp, scr, '', rr)
            rvi = rpi
            gosub layout
            w = f{'widgets', ni}
            rvw = w
         end
      end
      rpi = rvp{'pn'} + 0
   next rk
   w = f{'widgets', ni}
   return

* Step round the ring of widgets that can have the focus: step is 1 or -1
move.focus:
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   cur = f{'focus'} + 0
   ni = 0
   i = cur
   for k = 1 to nw
      i += step
      if i > nw then i = 1
      if i < 1 then i = nw
      gosub can.focus
      if cf and i # cur then ni = i ; exit
   next k
   if ni then gosub set.focus
   return

* A button was pressed (w): the form is done, or cancelled if it is the cancel button
press.button:
   if w{'cancel'} + 0 then
      ret = 'cancel' : @fm : w{'id'}
   end else
      ret = 'done' : @fm : w{'id'}
   end
   return

* Esc: the form is cancelled, and says which button is its cancel button
do.cancel:
   cid = ''
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      if w{'type'} = 'button' and w{'cancel'} + 0 then cid = w{'id'} ; exit
   next i
   ret = 'cancel' : @fm : cid
   return

* Return, said by a widget that is not a button: the default button, or the next widget
default.action:
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   dflt = 0
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      gosub on.page
      if w{'type'} = 'button' and w{'default'} + 0 and w{'disabled'} + 0 = 0 and ancdis = 0 and vis then dflt = i ; exit
   next i
   if dflt then
      w = f{'widgets', dflt}
      gosub press.button
   end else
      * 14 Oct 26: a form the program marked with f{'activate'} = 1 gives Return in a tree or a table to the program
      * as an event of its own (activate: the widget's id and its value), where it would otherwise move the focus on
      afi = f{'focus'} + 0
      if afi >= 1 and afi <= nw and f{'activate'} + 0 then
         aw = f{'widgets', afi}
         if aw{'type'} = 'tree' or aw{'type'} = 'table' then
            ret = 'activate' : @fm : aw{'id'} : @fm : aw{'value'}
            return
         end
      end
      step = 1
      gosub move.focus
      ret = 'handled'
   end
   return

* A key the focused widget had no use for (k2) or said done with a non-button
other.key:
   begin case
      case k2 = 'tab' or k2 = 'down'
         step = 1
         gosub move.focus
         ret = 'handled'
      case k2 = 'btab' or k2 = 'up'
         step = -1
         gosub move.focus
         ret = 'handled'
      case k2 = 'enter'
         gosub default.action
      case k2 = 'esc'
         gosub do.cancel
      case len(k2) = 1
         * a letter that no text widget took: the mnemonic of a button presses it
         ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : k2
         uk = upcase(k2)
         nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
         for i = 1 to nw
            w = f{'widgets', i}
            gosub on.page
            if w{'type'} = 'button' and w{'mn'} = uk and w{'disabled'} + 0 = 0 and ancdis = 0 and vis then
               gosub press.button
               exit
            end
         next i
      case 1
         ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : k2
   end case
   return

* The first control (in the order they were added) that is on the page, not disabled, and has this key as its ACCEL or, for an Alt-letter, as the letter
* marked with & in its text.  A label has no focus of its own: its letter takes the focus to the next control that can have it.  ni = its number, 0 if none.
find.accel:
   ni = 0
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      gosub on.page
      if vis and w{'disabled'} + 0 = 0 and ancdis = 0 and (w{'focusable'} + 0 = 1 or w{'type'} = 'label') then
         if w{'accel'} = key then ni = i
         if len(key) = 5 and key[1, 4] = 'alt-' and w{'amn'} # '' and w{'amn'} = upcase(key[5, 1]) then ni = i
         if ni > 0 then exit
      end
   next i
   if ni > 0 then
      w = f{'widgets', ni}
      if w{'type'} = 'label' then
         lab = ni
         ni = 0
         for k = 1 to nw
            lab += 1
            if lab > nw then lab = 1
            i = lab
            gosub can.focus
            if cf then ni = lab ; exit
         next k
         if ni = 0 then ni = -1                  ;* a label with no control to take the focus to: the key is used up, nothing happens
      end
   end
   return

* The accelerator found (find.accel: ni) is acted on: the control gets the focus, and then a button is pressed, a check box, slider or selector is
* turned over / moved to its next word, and any other control just has the focus.  A change is a change event (f{'achg'}), not only the focus event.
run.accel:
   ret = 'handled'
   if ni < 0 then return
   hit = ni
   if hit # f{'focus'} + 0 then gosub set.focus
   wi = hit
   w = f{'widgets', hit}
   wt = w{'type'}
   v1 = w{'value'}
   begin case
      case wt = 'button'
         gosub press.button
      case wt = 'check' or wt = 'slider' or wt = 'selector'
         wop = 'key' ; wkey = ' '
         gosub call.widget
         gosub after.widget
         if w{'value'} # v1 then f{'achg'} = hit
   end case
   gosub park.cursor
   return

route.key:
   if key = 'mouse' then
      gosub route.mouse
      return
   end
   if key = 'resize' then
      * The terminal's size changed ($sl_key says so).  This form's screen context is the live one (the kept one is only
      * updated when the statement ends), so it is made the new size and drawn again here, form and all; the key is then
      * passed on as one nobody used, which WAIT turns into the event resize.
      sw0 = scr<SL.S.W> ; sh0 = scr<SL.S.H>
      call $sl_resize(scr)
      * 19 Oct 26: a resize key with the size unchanged is the lift of the cursor lock ($sl_guard cleared the terminal and drew its own
      *   box): the terminal no longer matches the shadow, so the screen is drawn again from it, which also makes it match for what follows
      if scr<SL.S.W> = sw0 and scr<SL.S.H> = sh0 and scr<SL.S.OWNED> then call $sl_repaint(scr)
      ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
      return
   end
   if key = 'guardquit' then
      ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key               ;* the user left from the cursor lock ($sl_guardmode): no widget's key, the program's
      return
   end
   f{'achg'} = ''
   * an accelerator (S.75 TK-0.12): the key a control was given with ACCEL, or an Alt-letter that is the & letter of a button, check box, slider,
   * selector or label.  It goes to the control wherever the focus is, even in a text field, before the focused control sees the key.
   if len(key) >= 2 and (key[1, 4] = 'alt-' or key[1, 5] = 'ctrl-' or (key[1, 1] = 'f' and len(key) <= 3 and num(key[2, 9]))) then
      gosub find.accel
      if ni > 0 then
         gosub run.accel
         return
      end
   end
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   fi = f{'focus'} + 0
   if fi < 1 or fi > nw then
      k2 = key
      if key = 'esc' then gosub do.cancel else ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : key
      return
   end
   w = f{'widgets', fi}
   wi = fi
   wt = w{'type'}
   wop = 'key' ; wkey = key
   gosub call.widget
   gosub after.widget
   gosub park.cursor
   return

* A mouse event ($sl_mouse has it): the press of the left button, or the wheel, over a widget that can have the
* focus.  The widget under the pointer is the last one added that holds the cell (a later one is drawn over an
* earlier).  It gets the focus, then the event as op 'mouse' with the event as its key (kind, button, x, y, mods),
* and answers as it does to a key.  Anything else, and a click on nothing, is ignored.
route.mouse:
   call $sl_mouse('get', mev)
   ret = 'handled'
   mk = mev<1>
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   * the drag and the release that follow a press on a viewport's thumb are the viewport's wherever the pointer is
   dv = f{'drag'} + 0
   if dv > 0 and (mk = 'drag' or mk = 'release') then
      if dv <= nw then
         w = f{'widgets', dv}
         wi = dv
         wt = w{'type'}
         wop = 'mouse' ; wkey = mev
         gosub call.widget
         gosub after.widget
         if mk = 'release' or w{'drag'} = '' then f{'drag'} = 0
      end else
         f{'drag'} = 0
      end
      return
   end
   if not((mk = 'press' and mev<2> = 1) or mk = 'wheel') then return
   mx = mev<3> + 0
   my = mev<4> + 0
   hit = 0
   for i = nw to 1 step -1
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      gosub on.page
      if vis and w{'focusable'} + 0 = 1 and w{'disabled'} + 0 = 0 and ancdis = 0 then
         if mx >= w{'ax'} and mx < w{'ax'} + w{'w'} and my >= w{'ay'} and my < w{'ay'} + w{'h'} then
            cc = w{'clip'}
            if cc = '' then
               hit = i
            end else
               if mx >= cc<1, 1> and mx <= cc<1, 3> and my >= cc<1, 2> and my <= cc<1, 4> then hit = i
            end
            if hit then exit
         end
      end
   next i
   if hit = 0 then
      * a press of the left button on nothing: ignored, unless the program asked for it (f{'bgclick'} = 1, the IDE: the menu bar is not a widget)
      if mk = 'press' and f{'bgclick'} + 0 = 1 then ret = 'unhandled' : @fm : 'mouse'
      return
   end
   keepf = 0
   if mk = 'wheel' then gosub wheel.target
   if hit # f{'focus'} + 0 and keepf = 0 then
      ni = hit
      gosub set.focus
   end
   w = f{'widgets', hit}
   wi = hit
   wt = w{'type'}
   wop = 'mouse' ; wkey = mev
   gosub call.widget
   gosub after.widget
   if wt = 'viewport' and w{'drag'} # '' then f{'drag'} = hit
   gosub park.cursor
   return

* The wheel over a viewport, or over a widget in one that does not use the wheel itself (a list, memo, table, tree and
* scroll bar do), goes to the nearest viewport round it, and the focus stays where it is
wheel.target:
   w = f{'widgets', hit}
   wt = w{'type'}
   if wt = 'viewport' then
      keepf = 1
      return
   end
   if wt = 'list' or wt = 'memo' or wt = 'table' or wt = 'tree' or wt = 'scroll' then return
   wq = w{'pn'} + 0
   for wk = 1 to 32
      if wq = 0 then exit
      wp = f{'widgets', wq}
      if wp{'type'} = 'viewport' and wp{'disabled'} + 0 = 0 then
         hit = wq
         keepf = 1
         exit
      end
      wq = wp{'pn'} + 0
   next wk
   return

* What the form does with the answer (wr) of the widget w, of type wt, to a key or a click
after.widget:
   st = wr<1>
   k2 = wr<2>
   if wt = 'tabs' and f{'page'} # w{'value'} then
      f{'page'} = w{'value'}                 ;* another tab was chosen: the form shows its page
      gosub draw.all
   end
   if wt = 'viewport' and vmoved then
      vi = wi                                ;* a viewport scrolled: it and what is in it are drawn again
      gosub redraw.vp
   end
   begin case
      case st = 'handled'
         ret = 'handled'
      case st = 'done'
         if wt = 'button' then
            gosub press.button
         end else
            k2 = 'enter'
            gosub other.key
         end
      case st = 'cancel'
         gosub do.cancel
      case 1
         gosub other.key
   end case
   return

* The viewport number vi has scrolled (its sx, sy are new): the places are worked out again and its inside is blanked and
* drawn again with what is in it, and with whatever was added after it that lies over it, the focused widget last.  The rest of
* the form is not touched.  f{'scrolled'} tells WAIT.
redraw.vp:
   if unassigned(w) then svw = '' else svw = w
   if unassigned(wt) then svt = '' else svt = wt
   gosub layout
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   fi = f{'focus'} + 0
   vw = f{'widgets', vi}
   vx0 = vw{'ax'} + 0
   vy0 = vw{'ay'} + 0
   vx1 = vx0 + vw{'w'} - 1
   vy1 = vy0 + vw{'h'} - 1
   if vi = fi then
      w = vw
      gosub blank.inside
   end else
      di = vi
      gosub draw.one
   end
   for rj = vi + 1 to nw
      if rj # fi then
         dj = rj
         gosub redraw.member
         if rin then
            di = rj
            gosub draw.one
         end
      end
   next rj
   if fi >= 1 and fi <= nw then
      rin = 1
      if fi > vi then
         dj = fi
         gosub redraw.member
      end
      if rin then
         di = fi
         gosub draw.one
      end
   end
   gosub park.cursor
   f{'scrolled'} = vw{'id'} : @fm : vw{'sx'} : @vm : vw{'sy'}
   w = svw
   wt = svt
   return

* rin = 1 if widget number dj is inside viewport vi, or lies over its rectangle (vx0, vy0, vx1, vy1)
redraw.member:
   rin = 0
   gosub desc.of
   if isdesc then
      rin = 1
   end else
      mw = f{'widgets', dj}
      if mw{'ax'} <= vx1 and mw{'ax'} + mw{'w'} - 1 >= vx0 and mw{'ay'} <= vy1 and mw{'ay'} + mw{'h'} - 1 >= vy0 then rin = 1
   end
   return

* isdesc = 1 if widget number dj is inside widget number vi, at any depth
desc.of:
   isdesc = 0
   dq = dj
   for dk = 1 to 32
      dw = f{'widgets', dq}
      dq = dw{'pn'} + 0
      if dq = 0 then exit
      if dq = vi then
         isdesc = 1
         exit
      end
   next dk
   return

* Take widget number fw out of the form, and everything inside it.  ret = how many went.  The numbers of the widgets after
* it change, so each one's pn (the number of its container) and the form's focus are made right.
delete.widget:
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   dkill = ''
   for j = 1 to nw
      isk = 0
      if j = fw then
         isk = 1
      end else
         if j > fw then
            dw = f{'widgets', j}
            q = dw{'pn'} + 0
            if q > 0 then isk = dkill<q>
         end
      end
      dkill<j> = isk
   next j
   tmp = collection()
   tmp{'widgets'} = mat()
   newi = ''
   nn = 0
   gone = 0
   for j = 1 to nw
      if dkill<j> then
         newi<j> = 0
         gone += 1
         dw = f{'widgets', j}
         if dw{'id'} = f{'curparent'} then f{'curparent'} = ''
      end else
         nn += 1
         newi<j> = nn
         tmp{'widgets', nn} = f{'widgets', j}
      end
   next j
   f{'widgets'} = tmp{'widgets'}
   for j = 1 to nn
      dw = f{'widgets', j}
      q = dw{'pn'} + 0
      if q > 0 then dw{'pn'} = newi<q>
   next j
   ofoc = f{'focus'} + 0
   nf = 0
   if ofoc >= 1 and ofoc <= nw then nf = newi<ofoc>
   if nf = 0 then
      * the focused widget went: the focus goes to the first that can have it
      for i = 1 to nn
         gosub can.focus
         if cf then
            nf = i
            w = f{'widgets', i}
            w{'focused'} = 1
            exit
         end
      next i
   end
   f{'focus'} = nf
   f{'drag'} = 0
   nw = nn
   ret = gone
   if f{'shown'} then
      gosub init.page
      gosub layout
      gosub draw.all
   end
   return

run.modal:
   gosub show.form
   loop
      call $sl_key('', kk)
      if kk = '' or kk = 'guardquit' then kk = 'esc'
      key = kk
      gosub route.key
      st = ret<1>
   until st = 'done' or st = 'cancel'
   repeat

   result = ret
   gosub hide.form
   ret = result
   return

* Draw the form over the screen, keeping what is under it, with the focus on its first widget that can have it
* (or where an earlier run left it)
show.form:
   gosub hide.form                           ;* shown by an earlier WAIT: start again from the screen underneath
   gosub init.form
   gosub layout
   call $sl_region('save', scr, f{'x'} + 0, f{'y'} + 0, f{'w'} + 0, f{'h'} + 0, under)
   f{'under'} = under
   f{'shown'} = 1

   * the focus: where it was if that widget can have it, else the first that can
   nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
   start = f{'focus'} + 0
   first = 0
   for i = 1 to nw
      w = f{'widgets', i}
      w{'focused'} = 0
      gosub can.focus
      if cf and first = 0 then first = i
   next i
   i = start
   if i >= 1 and i <= nw then gosub can.focus else cf = 0
   if cf = 0 then start = first
   f{'focus'} = start
   if start then
      w = f{'widgets', start}
      w{'focused'} = 1
      ni = start
      if w{'pn'} + 0 > 0 then gosub reveal          ;* a widget in a viewport starts in view
   end

   gosub draw.all
   return

* One event: show the form if it is not shown, read keys until one of them means something to the program.
* tmo = seconds to wait for a key (null: for ever).  ret = 'event' : evt : eid : edata where evt is
*   button  (eid the button's id)           cancel  (Esc, eid null; or the form's cancel button, eid its id)
*   change  (eid, edata the new value: a check box, slider, selector, radio group, list or combo changed)
*   focus   (eid the widget the focus went to, edata the one it left)
*   key     (edata the key's name: one the form had no use for; also mouse, for a press of the left button on no widget, when the
*           program has set f{'bgclick'} = 1)    timeout    end (the input ended)
*   activate  (eid the tree's or table's id, edata its value: Return in one of them, only when the program has set
*             f{'activate'} = 1 and the form has no default button; otherwise Return moves the focus on)
wait.event:
   if not(f{'shown'}) then gosub show.form
   evt = ''
   eid = ''
   edata = ''
   f{'scrolled'} = ''
   gosub park.cursor                         ;* the statement before this one gave the cursor back to the program
   loop
      call $sl_key(tmo, kk)
      if kk = '' then
         evt = 'end'
         * 19 Oct 26: only the time running out is a timeout.  An input that has ended also gives a null key at once, and a
         * program that waits with a timeout (the IDE waits a second at a time) took it for the time passing and went round
         * again for ever, at full CPU.  $sl_key leaves STATUS() at ER$TIMEOUT when it was the time.
         if tmo # '' and status() = ER$TIMEOUT then evt = 'timeout'
      end else
         nw = inmat(f{'widgets'})
         fi0 = f{'focus'} + 0
         v0 = ''
         id0 = ''
         wt0 = ''
         if fi0 >= 1 and fi0 <= nw then
            w = f{'widgets', fi0}
            v0 = w{'value'}
            id0 = w{'id'}
            wt0 = w{'type'}
         end
         key = kk
         gosub route.key
         st = ret<1>
         fi1 = f{'focus'} + 0
         begin case
            case st = 'done'
               evt = 'button' ; eid = ret<2>
            case st = 'activate'
               evt = 'activate' ; eid = ret<2> ; edata = ret<3>
            case st = 'cancel'
               evt = 'cancel' ; eid = ret<2>
            case st = 'unhandled'
               evt = 'key' ; edata = ret<2>
               if edata = 'resize' then
                  evt = 'resize'                  ;* $sl_key has drawn the screen again at its new size
                  edata = @crtwide : @vm : @crthigh
               end
            case f{'achg'} # ''
               w = f{'widgets', f{'achg'}}              ;* an accelerator turned a check box, slider or selector over: a change, whether or not the focus moved
               evt = 'change' ; eid = w{'id'} ; edata = w{'value'}
            case fi1 # fi0 and fi1 >= 1
               w = f{'widgets', fi1}
               evt = 'focus' ; eid = w{'id'} ; edata = id0
            case fi0 >= 1 and (wt0 = 'check' or wt0 = 'slider' or wt0 = 'selector' or wt0 = 'radio' or wt0 = 'list' or wt0 = 'combo' or wt0 = 'tabs' or wt0 = 'table' or wt0 = 'tree' or wt0 = 'scroll')
               w = f{'widgets', fi0}
               if w{'value'} # v0 then
                  evt = 'change' ; eid = id0 ; edata = w{'value'}
               end
         end case
         * a viewport scrolled (a key, the wheel, a drag on its bar) and nothing else happened: that is a change, its value
         * the first column and row shown from 0, with a value mark between
         if evt = '' and f{'scrolled'} # '' then
            sc = f{'scrolled'}
            evt = 'change' ; eid = sc<1> ; edata = sc<2>
         end
         f{'scrolled'} = ''
      end
   until evt # ''
   repeat
   ret = 'event' : @fm : evt : @fm : eid : @fm : edata
   return
end

